## 5. Decorrelation check and convergence honesty

Per the L04 failure clause ("degenerate space → collapse to a single approach, note it"): the candidates are **not** degenerate, but they do converge on a shared core, and it is worth stating exactly where.

**Converged (forced by BC-1..BC-7 and CC-1..CC-2, not by ideation):** stage inserted between TRADEOFF and DESIGN; PLANNER RoleSpec with write scope `mitigation/` only; a non-empty `required_evidence` obligation; a catalogue artifact in the CAS carried to DESIGN over `planner_artifacts`; both edges through `Gate.propose_transition`; REMAND on failure; `runtime/mitigation.py` deleted or fully replaced. Anything that varies these is non-conforming, so ideation had no freedom there and correctly spent none.

**Genuinely decorrelated — the four fail on different axes:**

| | A (oracle) | B (stance) | C (substrate) | D (data model) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Enforcement lives in | a re-runnable checker | role separation | the topology table | the hand-off schema |
| Defeats always-passes (BC-3) | yes | yes | yes | yes |
| Defeats placeholder safeguards (CC-3) | no | partly (adversary attacks them) | no | no |
| Defeats self-marked severity (F-A2) | no | partly | no | **yes** |
| Satisfies CC-4 two-producer rule | n/a (deterministic only) | **yes** | n/a | n/a |
| Reduces recurrence of F2 systemically | no | no | **yes** | no |
| Blast radius | smallest | medium | largest | medium, on a *working* layer |
| Cost per run | 1 session | 2 sessions | 1 session | 1–2 sessions |
| Sealable this cycle | very likely | likely | uncertain | likely, if the frozen-doc question resolves |

The important structural observation: **A, C and D all leave adequacy unchecked; only B attacks it.** And **only C reduces the probability that the *next* layer goes missing.** Those two properties are orthogonal, which is why the composite in §6 is worth L06's attention rather than a straight pick.

